  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 837 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nAt the start of the new work week, a cut off low will be plunging\nthrough the southeast. The low looks to pass to our south on Monday,\nbefore dampening and dissolving into the larger scale troughing over\nFlorida on Tuesday. We currently look to be too far north of this \nfeature to see any significant impacts beyond just some increased \ncloud cover. \n\nBy Tuesday afternoon, mid level ridging will begin to build in from\nthe southwest, accompanied by surface high pressure building over the\nOhio Valley. Through the remainder of the week, subsidence from high\npressure will work to keep skies dry and clear. Under mostly clear\nskies, temps will enter a weak warming patter rising from highs in\nthe low 60s to start the week to the low 70s by Friday. Low will\nfollow a similar rebound warming from the 30s on Monday night to the\nmid 40s by Thursday night.",
